.Dd November 10, 2026
.Dt RASMEMSTAT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm rasmemstat
.Nd display the state of the rasmem RAS memory test suite (beta)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl m
.Op Fl V Ar view
.Op Fl a Ar seconds
.Op Fl s Cm e | a | t
.Op Fl w Ar seconds
.Op Fl -no-color
.Nm
.Fl 1
.Op Fl dFm
.Op Fl V Ar view
.Op Fl n Ar rows
.Op Fl s Cm e | a | t
.Nm
.Fl J
.Op Fl w Ar seconds
.Nm
.Fl f Ar dbfile
.Op Fl Jm
.Op Fl s Cm e | a | t
.Nm
.Fl v
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
shows the state of the
.Nm rasmem
kernel module.
On a terminal it runs full screen and refreshes every second; the
information is split into views selected with keys:
.Bl -tag -width "1 Overview"
.It Cm 1 No Overview
Health and its reasons, bad page counts, the current pass of the
periodic scan, boot test result, read-only checksums, database state,
a one-line coverage map and the worst bad pages.
.It Cm 2 No Map
The coverage map: all RAM in physical address order, one
.Ql #
per block, coloured by state:
bright green, fully tested (patterns, March C- and a retention hold on the
whole block, without an error, accumulated over passes and the boot test);
white, tested in the current pass;
pale orange, orange and dark orange, partly tested (50\(en90%, 10\(en50% and
under 10% of the block; the rest was in use);
purple, the same, but the untested part was free memory held in partly
used superpage reservations;
green, fully tested earlier but not yet reached in this pass;
grey, tested in the previous pass or at boot.
.Ql \&.
is never tested,
.Ql @
is where the scan is now, and
.Ql X
and
.Ql \&!
are bad pages, isolated or not.
Without colours the states are shown as
.Ql # ,
.Ql + ,
.Ql = ,
.Ql ~ ,
.Ql - ,
.Ql h ,
and
.Ql \&:
in that order.
Address gaps (holes) are left out; the row labels give the physical
address.
The scan visits memory in 8 MiB slots spread over all of RAM (see
.Va hw.rasmem.scan_order ) ,
so the blocks of the current pass are scattered over the map rather than
filling it from the bottom.
.It Cm 3 No Bad pages
Every recorded bad page with its class, state, module, error and retest
counters, how it was found and the data bits that flipped, followed by a
legend of the values shown.
.It Cm 4 No Modules
Memory modules from SMBIOS with their bad page counts.
.It Cm 5 No Details
Everything else: activity, rates, pass history, scan policy, in-use memory,
retries, allocator, retests, boot test phases and database.
.El
.Pp
Other keys:
arrows, PgUp, PgDn, Home and End scroll;
Tab and Left/Right cycle the views;
.Cm s
changes the sort order,
.Cm m
merges adjacent bad pages,
.Cm l
toggles the legend,
.Cm + No and Cm -
change the refresh interval,
.Cm r
refreshes now,
.Cm \&?
shows the keys and
.Cm q
quits.
.Pp
When the output is not a terminal, or with
.Fl 1 ,
.Nm
prints the overview and all bad pages (or the view chosen with
.Fl V )
instead.
Colors are used on a terminal unless
.Fl -no-color
is given or
.Ev NO_COLOR
is set.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl 1 , Fl -once
Print once and exit.
.It Fl V Ar view , Fl -view Ar view
The view to start with, or to print with
.Fl 1 :
.Cm overview , map , pages , modules , details
or
.Cm all .
.It Fl F , Fl -full
Print everything, as
.Fl V Cm all .
.It Fl J , Fl -json
JSON output.
Without
.Fl w ,
one pretty-printed document is printed.
With
.Fl w ,
one compact JSON object per line is printed every interval, suitable for
log shippers and monitoring agents.
Combined with
.Fl f ,
the database file is dumped as JSON.
.It Fl d , Fl -modules
List the memory modules, as
.Fl V Cm modules .
.It Fl f Ar dbfile , Fl -file Ar dbfile
Dump a database file written by the module (normally
.Pa /boot/rasmem.db )
without needing the module to be loaded.
.It Fl m , Fl -merge
Merge physically adjacent pages with the same class and state into one row.
.It Fl n Ar rows , Fl -rows Ar rows
Print at most
.Ar rows
bad pages.
.It Fl s Cm e | a | t , Fl -sort Cm e | a | t
Sort by error count (default), address or time of the last error.
.It Fl w Ar seconds , Fl -wait Ar seconds
Refresh interval (default 1).
.It Fl a Ar seconds , Fl -avg Ar seconds
Average the test rate over this many seconds (default 60).
The module tests in bursts every
.Va hw.rasmem.interval
milliseconds (1 s by default), so a short window shows mostly zero.
.It Fl v , Fl -version
Print the versions of
.Nm
and of the loaded kernel module, and exit.
.It Fl -no-color
Do not use ANSI colors.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent -compact
.It Pa /boot/rasmem.db
bad page database
.It Pa /boot/rasmem_blacklist.txt
page list for the loader's
.Va ram_blacklist
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mca 4 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
.Pp
The coverage map is read from
.Va hw.rasmem.map .
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in rasmem 0.1.0, a beta release
(the pre-release test builds were numbered 0.0.9b).
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Viktor Hlavaji Aq Mt davies@npulse.net ,
developed with the assistance of Claude (Anthropic), an AI assistant.
.Sh BUGS
rasmem is a beta test suite with limited testing on physical hardware.
On machines with ECC memory, errors corrected by the hardware are reported
by
.Xr mca 4
only; rasmem does not read them yet.
Please report problems with the output of
.Nm Fl J .
